// expect-error: NITPICK-TYPE-079
// expect-error-at: 21:5
// expect-error: NITPICK-TYPE-007
// expect-error-at: 27:5
// 2026-11-19 (landing 177d2d, row 10: the Bridge, form BR-5g, closing DEF-704, DEF-705, DEF-706, DEF-707 and DEF-712; rulings l.18410, l.19234,
// l.19307, l.19443, l.20202 and l.20254). A stub takes its bulk offset from the Bridge's own `ring_cap`, never from the region (DEF-704); refuses a
// call whose slots, slice bytes or return word don't fit the bulk area, as `OutOfBounds`, before any write (DEF-705); checks `closed` and `poisoned`
// first (DEF-706); `dispatch` range-checks the driver's indices before any arithmetic and kills a driver that rewrote line 0 (DEF-707); close and the
// reap clear the base and the stderr tail's cursor, and the tail refuses a closed Bridge (DEF-706, DEF-712); and every field of `Shm` and `Bridge` is
// `sealed` (D-313; DEF-467's fix for these two structs, l.19307). a probe of the seal (l.19443 item 1): a store in a named function's body. From seat
// AB's release hunt on BR-5f and BR-5g (l.19307, l.19443), `Team/TMP/atk-177d2d-bridge-2026-11-19/cells/ab/`, `seal_lambda.npk`, by `cat`, its `mod:`
// line and library path changed.
// seat AB (Ailp-team_215), 2026-11-19, seal route (closure): closures are removed (D-018). A "function value" in
// Nitpick is a reference to a named `func` with NO captured environment, so a Bridge reaches it only as a parameter
// and writing its sealed field happens in an ordinary function body, type-checked normally. This probe takes such a
// function as a value; the write `b.ring_cap = -1` is the field store the seal refuses. No capture back-door, no `wild`.
mod:bridge_seal_lambda;
use "../../../lib/nbridge.npk".*;

func:poke = NIL(Bridge->:b) never fails {
    b.ring_cap = 0i64 - 1i64;
    pass NIL;
};

func:caller = NIL(Bridge->:b) {
    func NIL(Bridge->) never fails:g = poke;
    drop raw g(b);
    pass NIL;
};

func:main = int32(cstring[]:_~argv) { exit 0i32; };
func:failsafe = int32(Error:_~e) { exit 1i32; };
